IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`

-- je54-gaps: what the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say, as questions a reader would ask, each answered by a refusal that says why.  Every function here refuses on every input: none of them has an answer in
-- any of the seven deposited texts (the provisions of each were searched for the words day, week, year, month, period, hour, zone, clock and time; the hits are the commencement provisions, the "midnight" and "month"
-- definitions, Article 7 and the phrase "for the time being"; the search is recorded in NOTES.md section 7).  Where the encoding needs the missing fact it takes it as an input (the time zone, the time at which a letter
-- would be delivered, the reading of fork I2); these functions are the places where a reader who asks for the fact itself is told that the Law does not give it.
-- The row for the calendar month, `the day one calendar month after`, is in je54-schedule-definitions, beside the Schedule definition of "month" that raises the question.

§ `Periods of days, weeks and years`

-- The functions in this module that have no @ref refuse because no provision exists to cite: the absence is the point.

GIVEN start IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      unit IS A `Unit of a period`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which a period that starts on a day ends` start n unit MEANS
    REFUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 has no rule for counting a period of days, weeks or years, and does not say what a day, a week or a year is"

§ `Time zone`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
`the time zone in which the Law reads a day` d MEANS
    REFUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 names no time zone in which a day is read; the caller states the zone, and this row assumes Jersey local time without the Law saying so"

§ `Service by post`

-- src:27 | Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, authorizes or requires any document to be served by post, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or “send”, or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the service shall be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting a letter containing the document, and, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 7 (src:27)
GIVEN posted IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which a letter posted on a day would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` posted MEANS
    REFUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say how long post takes or what the ordinary course of post is; the caller states the time at which the letter would be delivered"

§ `Commencement`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATETIME
`the time of day at which an enactment silent as to the time comes into force, if it is not the start of its day` made MEANS
    REFUSE "Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 give the start of the day and no other time of day; the Law gives no other"

-- src:187 | Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021
-- src:188 | L.8/2021
-- src:189 | 28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021)
-- src:190 | P.26/2021
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, row L.8/2021 (src:187-190)
GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which an enactment made on or after 28 September 2021 comes into force` made MEANS
    REFUSE "the commencement of an enactment made on or after 28 September 2021 is governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

-- src:137 | Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954
-- src:138 | L.17/1954
-- src:139 | 21 August 1954
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, row for the Law itself (src:137-139)
GIVETH A DATETIME
`the moment at which the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 came into force` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 gives no time of day for its own commencement on 21 August 1954"

§ `Bankruptcy`

-- src:29 | In every enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, references to a person becoming bankrupt shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as references to either –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 8 (src:29)
GIVEN event IS A DATE
      asked IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 8: the text that governs when the day of the event and the day the question is asked fall under different texts` event asked MEANS
    REFUSE "the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 does not say whether the text of Article 8 in force on the day of the event or on the day the question is asked governs; ask the function that takes a reading of fork I2"
